---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
// /privacy/: what this website and its public playground do with data. Website copy;
// the product's hosted data contract and the company notice are linked, not restated.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { COMPANY, COMPANY_PRIVACY, IMPRESSUM, LIVE_PLAYGROUND_WORKER, docPaths } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy and data" description="What the diffdevil website and public playground do with data: no accounts, no analytics, no stored analyses; public pull requests only." current="privacy">
  <article class="wrap privacy">
    <p class="eyebrow">#privacy</p>
    <h1 class="h2">Privacy and data</h1>
    <p class="lede">This page describes what the diffdevil website and its public playground do with data. The hosted GitHub App has its own <a class="link" href={docPaths.privacyAndData}>privacy and data contract</a>; the company notice is at <a class="link" href={COMPANY_PRIVACY} rel="noopener">{COMPANY}</a>.</p>
    <h2 class="h3">The website</h2>
    <ul class="small">
      <li>Static pages, no accounts, no sign-in, no analytics, no tracking pixels, no third-party scripts.</li>
      <li>No cookies. Your theme choice (system, dark or light) is kept in your browser's local storage under <code class="code-inline">diffdevil.theme</code> and never sent anywhere.</li>
      <li>Fonts (IBM Plex Sans and Mono) are served from this site; no request goes to a font network.</li>
      <li>The manual's search runs in your browser over an index built with the site.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="h3">The playground</h2>
    <ul class="small">
      <li>Curated examples are analyzed in your browser from files shipped with the site. Nothing is sent to a server when you open one or edit its policy.</li>
      <li>When you analyze a public pull request, your browser asks the playground API (<code class="code-inline">{LIVE_PLAYGROUND_WORKER}</code> in production) to read that public pull request from GitHub and return the analysis. The API accepts public <code class="code-inline">github.com</code> pull-request URLs only, never asks for a token, performs no repository writes, and stores no analysis history. GitHub's unauthenticated read allowance is shared by the API's visitors; when it is exhausted the API says so instead of inventing a result.</li>
      <li>The edited policy travels in the page URL so a result can be shared and reloaded. It is not stored by the site.</li>
      <li>"Carry into the GitHub App" passes the policy in the URL of the App page; nothing from the playground session is kept.</li>
      <li>Short-lived rate-limit and cache controls on the API are abuse and compute protection, not an activity timeline. Raw client addresses and entered URLs are not retained in product analytics.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="h3">Agent Skill and setup instructions</h2>
    <p class="small">The skill and setup files are plain Markdown served from this site. Fetching them tells us nothing beyond an ordinary page request; the site does not identify the agent or the user.</p>
    <h2 class="h3">Contact and legal</h2>
    <p class="small">Legal notice: <a class="link" href={IMPRESSUM} rel="noopener">Impressum</a>. Security reports: <a class="link" href="/docs/security/">Security</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  .privacy { max-width: 760px; padding: 40px 0 64px; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .privacy .eyebrow, .privacy .lede { margin: 0; }
  .privacy h2 { margin-top: 18px; }
  .privacy ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 8px; color: var(--fg-2); }
  .privacy p.small { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-2); }
</style>
